  "slug": "lsst-gravitational-waves-66df",
  "summary": "Seven preprints from 12–19 November 2026 supply emulators, differentiable codes and new probes for survey-era analyses of structure, dark energy and gravity.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is modeling infrastructure for survey-era inference. A Hi-COLA-trained emulator gives the nonlinear matter power spectrum in Cubic Galileon gravity for LSST Year 1 weak lensing and clustering. bihalofit-JAX provides a differentiable, open-source nonlinear bispectrum and projected statistics, reported to run orders of magnitude faster than existing approaches. A cubic-order EFT forward model of the Lyman-alpha forest, validated on CAMELS and Sherwood, yields BAO shift predictions and simulation-based priors. A second thread uses alternative probes: a physics-informed neural network reconstructs the dark energy equation of state and growth index from DESI DR2 and other data to test GR, while fast radio bursts constrain baryon distribution with IllustrisTNG and Ωm–w from 125 localized bursts. The QCD equation-of-state study of early-universe expansion and stochastic gravitational waves is peripheral to this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
